WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:05.420
<b>This is a work of fiction. The names of the people, places, and organizations
are fictitious and in no way related to any real person or entity.</b>

00:10.890 --> 00:11.740
Impossible...

00:12.690 --> 00:13.720
Why?

00:16.330 --> 00:18.000
So that's how it is.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.770
Deer's Den is on the move... Shikanoko Noko!

00:23.100 --> 00:27.130
<i>The hunch that the legendary Matagi hunter 
Kumatori Soichiro had was correct.</i>

00:27.130 --> 00:28.110
<b>Hokkaido</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:28.110
<b>Nara Prefecture</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:28.110
<b>Nagasaki Prefecture</b>

00:27.570 --> 00:31.380
<i>Unbeknownst to all, the wrath of the deer 
was concentrating upon Hino City.</i>

00:30.360 --> 00:31.380
<b>Hino City</b>

00:33.590 --> 00:37.090
<i>And now, a huge deer storm 
is about to wreak havoc!</i>

02:07.980 --> 02:12.980
<b>Farewell Nokotan!?
Long Live the Deer Club!</b>

02:13.200 --> 02:15.610
S-Say what now?!

02:16.770 --> 02:18.370
This is bad, Koshitan!

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>4/10/2024 3:45 PM</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>Dear Nokotan-sama,</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>Thank you for everything last week.
This is Kumatori.
It is a chilly day here in Hokkaido.</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>The other day at Daisetsuzan,
I happened to run into an assassin
who is probably after you. It appears
as though Deer's Den is sending
assassins from all over Japan
to eradicate you.</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>I pray that you are safe
from the bottom of my heart.</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:20.820
<b>Sincerely, Kumatori Soichiro</b>

02:18.370 --> 02:22.830
Kumatori-san just sent me a DM saying that
 Deer's Den assassins are coming to Hino City!

02:22.830 --> 02:24.040
Hang on a damn minute!

02:24.040 --> 02:26.250
I have <i>several</i> questions!

02:26.720 --> 02:27.830
Onee-chan?

02:29.490 --> 02:32.630
Who's Shikanoko?

02:33.310 --> 02:33.930
Huh?

02:34.630 --> 02:39.290
What happened to that serious-looking stinger 
that was supposed to lead into the finale?

02:39.290 --> 02:41.290
That doesn't matter right now!

02:41.290 --> 02:43.010
It doesn't matter?!

02:43.010 --> 02:44.360
<i>It really doesn't.</i>

02:44.360 --> 02:46.570
Deer's Den, huh...

02:46.570 --> 02:48.390
You've heard of them, Anko?

02:49.210 --> 02:52.230
You're familiar with the local mascots 
created to promote various cities?

02:52.670 --> 02:57.360
Well, there's a secret organization that 
specializes in training the deer-type ones:

02:57.360 --> 02:59.650
Deer's Den.

02:59.650 --> 03:02.160
What's with this secret 
organization outta nowhere?!

03:02.160 --> 03:04.120
<i>Just Anime Finale Things.</i>

03:04.490 --> 03:07.480
You see, that's where I'm from.

03:07.480 --> 03:12.000
But the training became a real pain in the—
I mean, I had important reasons for leaving.

03:12.350 --> 03:15.000
Why are you adding more random plot points?

03:15.000 --> 03:17.130
<i>This, too, is Just Anime Finale Things.</i>

03:17.420 --> 03:20.630
They've been able to determine my 
location by watching the anime as it airs.

03:20.630 --> 03:24.760
And now, they're dispatching assassins 
to bring me back as a traitor!

03:25.370 --> 03:29.270
Right... So you're saying a bunch 
of local mascots are after you?

03:29.270 --> 03:33.480
Come on, now. They're not going to arrange 
celebrity appearances for an anime like—

03:35.980 --> 03:38.050
There's one right in front of us!

03:39.210 --> 03:40.530
You're Kyun-chan.

03:40.530 --> 03:46.780
<b>Hokkaido Map</b>

03:41.570 --> 03:44.380
Kyun-chan grew up in the Daisetsuzan 
National Park in Hokkaido.

03:44.380 --> 03:46.780
Timid but curious,

03:47.110 --> 03:49.910
they came down from the mountain 
to learn about various things

03:49.910 --> 03:53.990
and ended up becoming a local mascot 
to promote the attractions of Hokkaido.

03:55.350 --> 03:57.540
I can't believe we get to meet them in Hino.

03:57.540 --> 04:00.090
No, really. How do you know all these things?

04:00.090 --> 04:04.020
Speaking of Hokkaido, they produce 
some of the best rice in Japan—

04:04.020 --> 04:05.220
You can shut up.

04:05.700 --> 04:09.520
Kyun-chan. I'm not going back to Deer's Den.

04:09.520 --> 04:12.630
I have a new life now as 
Shikanoko Noko of the Deer Club!

04:13.610 --> 04:17.230
Let us battle for the freedom 
of the deer, Kyun-chan!

04:19.530 --> 04:21.760
They seem happy that you'll play with them.

04:21.760 --> 04:24.990
Bashame's gonna go check on her rice field.

04:24.990 --> 04:29.760
<b>1st Hinominami High School
Chitty Chitty Nokotan vs Kyun-chan
Dance King Competition!!</b>

04:25.390 --> 04:29.760
This is the Nokotan versus Kyun-chan 
Dance King Competition!

04:31.280 --> 04:33.270
This is the set from episode 2!

04:33.270 --> 04:35.610
Also, why a dance competition?

04:35.040 --> 04:37.790
<b></b>Producer
<b>Koshi Anko</b>

04:35.610 --> 04:37.790
And what am I even doing here?!

04:38.210 --> 04:42.920
Nokotan and Kyun-chan will dance at the 
same time, and the better dancer will win!

04:42.920 --> 04:44.800
Now, if Nokotan loses...

04:44.800 --> 04:49.740
<b>Right to Deport</b>

04:45.130 --> 04:47.420
She will be forcefully 
deported back to Deer's Den.

04:47.420 --> 04:49.930
But if she wins, she gets a 
year's supply of deer crackers!

04:49.930 --> 04:51.020
This again?!

04:51.350 --> 04:53.270
And the judge will be...

04:53.760 --> 04:55.520
Tsunoda-san!

04:55.520 --> 04:57.760
This is messed up!

04:57.760 --> 05:01.530
<i>Her secret already came out at the sports 
festival, so Koshitan's not holding back.</i>

05:02.330 --> 05:04.650
Shikanoko, can you actually win?

05:04.650 --> 05:08.660
Leave it to me! I'm known as the 
legendary dancer of Deer's Den!

05:09.230 --> 05:13.290
I'm excited to find out just how much 
Kyun-chan's polished their antlers.

05:13.610 --> 05:15.130
Okay...

05:15.130 --> 05:16.960
Start dancing!

05:28.950 --> 05:30.430
<b>Choreography: Lucky Ikeda</b>

05:30.430 --> 05:32.380
Kyun-chan!

05:32.380 --> 05:33.910
Kyun-chan was so on point.

05:33.910 --> 05:35.810
They're so cute that my heart hurts.

05:36.230 --> 05:38.560
<i>As for Kumatori Soichiro...</i>

05:39.390 --> 05:40.560
So cute.

05:41.060 --> 05:42.640
And yet we have...

05:42.640 --> 05:44.930
Not bad, Kyun-chan.

05:45.840 --> 05:48.320
Your skin's so thick, it's legendary.

05:48.320 --> 05:51.090
<b></b>Judge
<b>Tsunoda-san</b>

05:48.670 --> 05:51.420
All right. If our judge could 
begin his deliberations...

05:52.580 --> 05:54.700
The winner is Kyun-chan!

05:54.850 --> 05:56.710
<b>1st Hinominami High School
Chitty Chitty Nokotan vs Kyun-chan
Dance King Competition!!</b>

05:58.800 --> 06:00.960
How could you possibly think you won?

06:00.960 --> 06:04.210
<b></b>Judge
<b>Tsunoda-san</b>

06:01.400 --> 06:04.210
Also, I guess you actually 
deliberated properly, Tsunoda-san.

06:04.210 --> 06:05.730
Curse you, Tsunoda!

06:05.730 --> 06:07.680
This is the problem with you stupid deer!

06:07.680 --> 06:10.220
You realize you're also a deer, don't you?

06:10.490 --> 06:12.100
<b>Employees of Deer's Den</b>

06:12.420 --> 06:14.600
I don't wanna go back to Deer's Den!

06:14.880 --> 06:19.100
I'm gonna keep being taken care of by 
the Deer Club and live the easy life!

06:19.100 --> 06:21.340
You're the worst, you know that?

06:21.340 --> 06:23.770
But what can we do? You lost fair and square.

06:24.770 --> 06:28.890
I don't think we can keep having 
a Deer Club with no actual deer.

06:28.890 --> 06:31.410
Oh, you'll need to pay back those club funds.

06:32.600 --> 06:35.080
This ain't over yet!

06:35.080 --> 06:39.790
If you intend on taking her back... 
You'll have to face me, Kyun-chan!

06:41.250 --> 06:43.880
Koshitan... You care that much about Nokotan?

06:44.100 --> 06:46.920
Koshitan... You're doing all this for me?

06:46.920 --> 06:48.130
<i>She is not.</i>

06:48.130 --> 06:50.850
We have a surprise second round!

06:50.850 --> 06:54.140
Our new challenger will be the 
Deer Club president, Koshi Torako!

06:54.450 --> 06:56.640
<i>I guess I've gotta do this!</i>

06:56.640 --> 06:58.580
Start dancing!

07:14.190 --> 07:17.660
<i>To think that my DeerColle experience 
would pay off here...</i>

07:18.010 --> 07:20.040
You're wonderful, Onee-chan!

07:20.040 --> 07:22.810
<b></b>Judge
<b>Tsunoda-san</b>

07:20.310 --> 07:22.970
All right. If our judge could 
begin his deliberations...

07:23.060 --> 07:24.290
<b>Draw</b>

07:24.290 --> 07:26.670
Wow! We've got a draw!

07:26.670 --> 07:28.920
<b>Draw</b>

07:26.890 --> 07:28.930
In which case...

07:29.300 --> 07:31.260
<b></b>Judge
<b>Tsunoda-san</b>

07:29.300 --> 07:31.260
<b></b>Judge
<b>Nokotan</b>

07:30.750 --> 07:32.680
Your antlers just aren't there yet.

07:32.680 --> 07:33.680
<b>Spicy</b>

07:33.680 --> 07:35.580
Want me to pull out them antlers?!

07:35.580 --> 07:40.350
Now, now. At least we know that Nokotan's 
not being forcefully deported.

07:42.310 --> 07:44.650
You've gotten stronger, Kyun-chan.

07:45.480 --> 07:47.730
You've completely lost, by the way.

07:47.730 --> 07:50.650
To celebrate your growth... Have this.

07:50.650 --> 07:54.050
Kyun-chan's a rabbit. 
Can they eat deer crackers?

07:54.050 --> 07:55.030
Huh?

07:55.680 --> 08:00.470
Specifically, a northern pika, a species 
known for its round ears and eyes.

08:00.470 --> 08:05.590
They're quiet and timid, so they 
usually wear a Yezo sika hood.

08:05.590 --> 08:11.920
But they're quite curious, so sometimes, 
they wear other hoods, too.

08:13.000 --> 08:15.930
You're not a deer... 
but you belong to Deer's Den?

08:16.390 --> 08:19.090
Man... I worked up a good sweat.

08:19.090 --> 08:20.680
What actually makes a deer?

08:21.530 --> 08:23.060
Nokotan!

08:23.420 --> 08:25.990
Play with us next, hana!

08:25.990 --> 08:27.600
Wait, now there's more?!

08:28.070 --> 08:29.940
The next assassins already showed up...

08:29.940 --> 08:32.190
Chikamaru-kun and Hana-chan.

08:33.240 --> 08:35.810
They're local mascots from 
Ojika Town in Nagasaki Prefecture,

08:35.810 --> 08:38.640
a boy and a girl who work hard 
to make as many smiles as they can

08:38.640 --> 08:44.500
bloom like flowers on the island of Ojika 
to bring people closer to Ojika Town.

08:45.580 --> 08:46.870
Hello, chika!

08:46.870 --> 08:49.100
Oh, hi. You're so polite...

08:49.960 --> 08:51.480
By the way, these are kids

08:51.480 --> 08:55.060
who are wearing costumes inspired 
by sika deer from Kyushu.

08:55.060 --> 08:56.590
Again, they're not even deer?!

08:56.950 --> 09:01.450
Now that we have some new assassins, 
we'll be doing a 2v2 duo competition!

09:01.450 --> 09:03.730
They'll be playing a mind-reading game!

09:03.870 --> 09:11.230
<b>1st Hinominami High School
Chitty Chitty Nokotan vs Kyun-chan
Dance King Competition!!</b>

09:05.280 --> 09:08.660
Without saying anything, you'll have 
to guess what your partner is thinking

09:08.660 --> 09:11.230
to show just how strong 
your love for each other is!

09:11.690 --> 09:13.500
Let's do our best, Koshitan!

09:13.500 --> 09:16.040
Let's show everyone just 
how strong our bond is!

09:16.040 --> 09:18.490
At this rate, bring anything on!

09:18.490 --> 09:23.160
Okay, please guess what 
the other is thinking.

09:23.160 --> 09:25.250
Ready... Go!

09:25.920 --> 09:28.880
Ojika Town is made up of a 
number of big and little islands

09:28.880 --> 09:31.970
that are in the ocean west of Kyushu, chika.

09:29.230 --> 09:31.860
<b>Ojika Town</b>

09:31.970 --> 09:36.260
The main industries there are fishing, 
farming, and tourism, chika.

09:36.260 --> 09:40.250
The ruins on Nozaki Island have been 
chosen as a World Heritage Site

09:40.250 --> 09:43.690
and there's plenty to see there 
since it's so full of nature, hana.

09:43.690 --> 09:46.140
That's what she's thinking, chika.

09:43.690 --> 09:46.140
That's what he's thinking, hana.

09:46.140 --> 09:47.640
Correct!

09:47.640 --> 09:50.010
Uh, that was just their standard tourism spiel?

09:50.010 --> 09:52.400
Also, this is clearly just guessing!

09:52.400 --> 09:54.790
I don't know anything about that.

09:54.790 --> 09:58.410
They got it perfectly right... 
That's amazing.

09:58.860 --> 10:01.670
Koshitan, we're up next!

10:01.670 --> 10:03.180
R-Right...

10:04.670 --> 10:06.410
Ready, go!

10:12.840 --> 10:14.760
And now, if you'll answer!

10:14.760 --> 10:15.420
Okay!

10:15.670 --> 10:17.790
I love you, Nokotan.

10:17.790 --> 10:23.100
I spent three months' pay 
to get you these... antlers.

10:23.460 --> 10:26.020
Oh, Koshitan!

10:26.020 --> 10:27.560
Woo, woo, chika!

10:27.820 --> 10:29.190
Incorrect.

10:29.640 --> 10:33.770
The thing Onee-chan is always 
thinking about is me.

10:34.230 --> 10:37.820
No, it's me! Koshitan, answer.

10:38.160 --> 10:41.530
Uh... Yeah, I've got no idea.

10:41.530 --> 10:43.120
That's so mean, Koshitan!

10:43.120 --> 10:45.660
How the hell would I know?! I'm no psychic!

10:45.660 --> 10:48.940
Does this mean you don't have 
an answer? Which means...

10:48.940 --> 10:51.890
Chikamaru-kun and Hana-chan win!

10:51.890 --> 10:53.210
Yay!

10:53.210 --> 10:56.210
Wah! I don't wanna go!

10:56.210 --> 10:58.650
Did you need our help?

10:58.650 --> 11:00.150
You're Shikayamada Shika!

11:00.150 --> 11:01.510
It's Nekoyamada Neko!

11:01.510 --> 11:03.390
What are you doing here, Nekoyamada-san?

11:03.390 --> 11:06.880
As the student council, it's our 
duty to protect the students.

11:06.880 --> 11:09.090
It's not for you or anything, President.

11:09.450 --> 11:12.580
<i>Usually, Neko-chan would be more than 
happy to see the Deer Club disbanded,</i>

11:12.580 --> 11:14.900
<i>but since it's the final 
episode of the anime...</i>

11:15.830 --> 11:17.440
<i>She's been standing by the whole time.</i>

11:17.440 --> 11:19.240
You don't need to include that 
in the narration!

11:19.500 --> 11:21.800
Did you want to play with us, too, chika?

11:21.800 --> 11:26.920
Yes! You can count on me. This game 
is perfect for the student council.

11:26.920 --> 11:29.910
We can understand each other 
without saying a word.

11:30.460 --> 11:32.460
Okay, Kinu. Pair up with me.

11:32.920 --> 11:35.670
<i>I won't let them take Nokotan-senpai.</i>

11:35.920 --> 11:40.300
<i>I-I-I need to throw my life away for Chiharu, 
since she paired up with me!</i>

11:42.320 --> 11:42.970
I get it.

11:43.300 --> 11:44.180
Please don't!

11:44.490 --> 11:49.060
Okay, now that we have our new 
competitors, let's start round 2!

11:52.860 --> 11:54.620
Oh, it's already time, chika.

11:54.620 --> 11:58.580
Today's the birthday of Uemura Reo-kun, 
who lives in Ojika Town, chika!

11:58.580 --> 12:00.460
We're heading back to celebrate, hana.

12:00.460 --> 12:01.070
Huh?

12:01.440 --> 12:03.070
Oh, that's right.

12:03.490 --> 12:05.810
Whenever a child has a birthday in Ojika Town,

12:05.810 --> 12:08.370
Chikamaru-kun and Hana-chan 
come to celebrate.

12:08.720 --> 12:10.500
Bye-bye, chika!

12:08.760 --> 12:10.500
Bye-bye, hana!

12:10.980 --> 12:13.210
We won... Everyone!

12:13.210 --> 12:15.540
No, you keep losing.

12:15.540 --> 12:17.370
That was a rough battle.

12:17.370 --> 12:20.030
You <i>really</i> haven't done anything.

12:20.030 --> 12:21.300
Oh, here.

12:21.840 --> 12:25.180
It's from some really pale old guy.

12:29.470 --> 12:31.810
Wait... Does that mean <i>he's</i> coming?

12:32.260 --> 12:34.630
Seriously, another one?

12:34.630 --> 12:36.240
Who is it this time?

12:37.440 --> 12:44.820
During the next break, Deer's Den's 
finest assassin will come to Hino...

12:44.820 --> 12:46.910
It's Sento-kun!

12:50.090 --> 12:53.710
Wh-What?!

12:53.960 --> 12:57.460
<i>The ultimate battle for the 
Deer Club is about to begin!</i>

12:57.460 --> 13:00.960
<b>Kagoshima
Kirishima
Mount Karakuni</b>

13:00.960 --> 13:04.470
<b>Kagoshima
Kirishima Miyama Kirishima
Shikagahara</b>

13:04.470 --> 13:06.470
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

13:05.420 --> 13:06.470
"Dear Nokotan.

13:06.790 --> 13:09.290
I'll be dropping in on you next break.

13:09.290 --> 13:12.370
Catch me at the Hino Municipal Gym.

13:12.370 --> 13:13.480
From Sento."

13:13.870 --> 13:15.980
This is undoubtedly a challenge letter.

13:15.980 --> 13:18.100
Maybe he's just literally dropping by?

13:20.410 --> 13:23.590
I-I-I'll easily take on any challenge!

13:23.590 --> 13:26.530
Calm down! And you've 
lost every match so far!

13:26.530 --> 13:28.580
Bring it on!

13:28.580 --> 13:30.580
What even are those punches?

13:31.940 --> 13:34.990
We're training! We're training right now!

13:34.990 --> 13:35.920
Let's go!

13:37.030 --> 13:42.340
Welp... Looks like my sister's 
shonen manga button has been pushed.

